# ⛔⛔ SCREEN CAPTURES AND ANY OTHER VIDEO. Kevin recorded the clip that went with
# the first public post to `data/` on 2026-10-04: 50.5MB, 2920x1926, ~23 Mbps —
# FORTY-SIX TIMES the largest file this repo tracks, and one `git add -A` from
# being in history forever, where nothing can take it out again.
#
# ⚠️ THE PRECEDENT IS EIGHT LINES UP. `builders/build_rules.py` "was swept onto
# the remote by a `git add -A` in 3061347 and removed in the commit that
# follows", and that entry exists so it could not happen a third time. This is
# the same hazard with a much bigger file, and `git add -A` is how every commit
# in this repo is made.
#
# ⭐ THE SITE SHIPS NO VIDEO AND IS NOT ABLE TO. The league's highlight is reached
# through an iframe built on open and torn down on close (see `drawClip`) — a
# BUTTON, never an embed, which is the whole bargain that feature was allowed on.
# So no video file can ever be a build input, and `src/card.png` is unaffected:
# this names video extensions only, and the sharing card is a PNG.
*.mp4
*.mov
*.m4v
*.webm
